  "hash_binding": "This evidence is finalized before root verification and is itself hashed in that receipt. The final attestation binds receipt bytes, final snapshot and evidence bytes without a circular self-hash. build/ is gitignored, so build/audit files are bound here rather than by the snapshot.",
  "proof_route": [
    "exists_contDiff_one_eqOn_ball: multiply by a ContDiffBump supported inside O; ContDiff is checked pointwise, on O by the product rule and off the topological support by local vanishing",
    "second countability (TopologicalSpace.isOpen_iUnion_countable) extracts a countable subfamily of those balls covering O, and Set.Countable.exists_eq_range indexes it by natural numbers",
    "disjointed turns S intersected with the balls into countably many pairwise disjoint measurable pieces whose union is S, each contained in one ball",
    "graphMap_injective makes the images of the pieces pairwise disjoint and measurableSet_image_graphMap makes them measurable, so lintegral_iUnion applies on both sides",
    "on each piece the pre-existing global theorem applies to the local C1 representative, and Filter.EventuallyEq.gradient_eq transfers the gradient because the two functions agree on an OPEN ball around each point of the piece"
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "L9 regular-part C1 coarea, which additionally needs the t-parametrized C1 implicit function family, the same-dimensional Jacobian change of variables and the cancellation of |det DPhi| = |Du(e)| against sqrt(1 + norm of D_y psi squared) = norm of grad u over |Du(e)|",
    "L11 general C1 weighted coarea and L12 the Lipschitz version",
    "the weighted coarea EQUALITY Analysis.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet and its C1 specialization Isoperimetry.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet, both still direct holes",
    "L6/L6a/L7 Whitney C1 extension from a closed set and exact C1 pieces; this round's localization is interior only",
    "sharp C^(finrank) Analysis.sard (no downstream consumer) and Analysis.ae_forall_fderiv_ne_zero, both still carrying sorryAx",
    "sharpness of the Eilenberg constant",
    "smoothConstant_le_minkowskiConstant",
    "smoothConstant_mul_lintegral_min_superlevel_le",
    "equality of the two Cheeger constants"
  ],
